# Phase discipline

Read [docs/master-spec.md](docs/master-spec.md) and the current phase doc before changing code.

Work only on the current phase. Phase 1 through Phase 8 are complete. See [docs/phase-8.md](docs/phase-8.md). Phase 9 is the TradingView door. See [docs/phase-9.md](docs/phase-9.md).

Feature work happens on `develop`. Merge to `main` only when the user is ready for production.

Phase 8 is the Futures strategy on Bybit (USDT linear perp buy / sell / close). Phase 9 adds a per-book HTTPS webhook into `runFuturesCommand`. Do not add a Fly.io worker. Do not call private exchange APIs from the browser. Paper accounts still use the in-app ledger.

Do not create later-phase tables or speculative architecture. Do not start typed desks, Hyperliquid, or MEXC/XT until Phase 9 is accepted.

Keep dependencies minimal. Prefer the simplest solution that satisfies the current phase.

Stop at the end of the phase. After acceptance criteria pass, report results and wait for instruction.
